review_comments.body:
**Suggestion: log when a different master key is silently ignored**

`install_master_key` uses `let _ = MASTER_KEY.set(key)` which silently ignores any subsequent call with a *different* key. While the doc comment says "installing the same key again (e.g. from tests) is a no-op", the actual behavior is that installing *any* key after the first succeeds silently. Consider adding a debug-level log when a different key is discarded:

```rust
if let Err(_) = MASTER_KEY.set(key) {
    if MASTER_KEY.get() != Some(&key) {
        tracing::debug!("ignoring attempt to install a different master key");
    }
}
```

